# Data licence

The benchmark data in this repository is dedicated to the public domain under
CC0 1.0 Universal. Full text: LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt

## Scope

CC0-1.0 applies to the measurement artefacts:

    results/**                          v1 per-request JSON
    analysis/summary.csv
    analysis/summary_by_config.csv
    analysis/verbose_accounting.json
    v2_3090_followup/**/*.log           v2 raw llama-cli logs
    v2_3090_followup/results_v2.json
    v2_3090_followup/n3_results_20260426.json
    v2_3090_followup/exp2_codejson_n3/results.json
    v2_3090_followup/exp2_codejson_n3/master.log
    v3_dflash_2026_05_07/data/**
    v4_audit_2026_08_25/data/**        the 2026-08-25/26 controlled tier:
                                       per-arm-run JSON, manifests, run markers,
                                       GPU telemetry CSV, checkpoint timer
                                       extractions and log SHA-256 manifests
    analysis/*.json                     derived aggregates, including
    analysis/*.csv                      plot_data.json and the counter comparison

The v4 tier was added on 2026-08-25 and this list did not name it until
2026-08-26, which left 601 committed measurement files without a stated
licence. They are CC0-1.0 like every other measurement here.

Everything else - code, shell scripts, Markdown, and the generated charts -
is MIT, see LICENSE.

## Not covered

The model weights are not distributed here and are not covered by this
licence. `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf`, `Qwen3.5-0.8B-Q4_K_M.gguf`, the
DFlash drafter and the MTP head carry their own upstream terms; see the Qwen,
unsloth and z-lab model cards.

`v4_audit_2026_08_25/patches/checkpoint_timers.patch` is a diff against
llama.cpp and carries llama.cpp's MIT licence, not this repository's.

Raw logs contain model output generated during benchmarking. That text is
included as measurement evidence and inherits whatever terms apply to the
model that produced it.
